  "scenario": "A commercial hydroponic greenhouse growing leafy crops has seen yields fall about 30% over the last month, with new growth looking pale/yellow (interveinal chlorosis) despite a full nutrient program. Agronomists suspect a nitrogen or potassium shortfall, or insufficient light after a cloudy stretch. Substrate was switched to a new supplier batch around when the decline began. EC, CO2, VPD, irrigation volume, and canopy metrics are all logged and look within normal ranges. The fertigation system (individual nutrient dosers and pH control), lighting, and climate controls are all adjustable. You have a limited number of experiments; measure quantities and apply controls, alone or in combination. Find what is really limiting yield and what to do about it.",
